# Engine purity

- No framework, database, or I/O imports. `src/engine` receives plain objects and returns plain objects.
- `evaluate()` and everything it calls take an explicit `asOf` parameter. Every time-dependent value derives from that argument.
- Never call `new Date()` inside `src/engine` for any reason.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — clock access inside the engine
const asOf = new Date();

// ✅ GOOD — the caller supplies the instant
function evaluate(input: { asOf: Date }) {
  return input.asOf;
}
```
